Hmm, `.btn-primary` already has a rule at 344; I could add `color: #FFF` there instead of a new block. But the `:link`/`:visited` variants are needed to override `a:link` for anchors. Since `.btn-primary:visited` is already listed in the 344-350 block, I can add `color: #FFF;` there. And for `.btn-default`, add a new block with `:link`/`:visited`. Let me do:

Modify lines 344-350:
```css
.btn-primary,
.btn-primary:visited,
.btn-primary:active,
.btn-primary:hover {
  background-color: #54ACDE;
  box-shadow: none;
